(533, 'A1', $t$Hold a judge's [L2] gloss to the KJV renderings of its number (K-GLS), TRIAL$t$,
 $t$A judge's [L2] gloss on a COLLISION POINTS line is held to the KJV's own renderings of that Strong's number. When a gloss part holds no KJV rendering of its number (for example "to cohabit conjugally" for G4905), the engine sends the judge one TRIAL item that quotes the part and lists the number's KJV renderings, and asks the judge to restate the line on those renderings or retract it. The item voids nothing and sets no count; a retraction that answers only K-GLS items is recorded, not applied (rev 1a). Expected: in 41418, judgments 1263 and 1265 each get a K-GLS item on D5 vs C2 for G4905. (ask533/w1/plan533.md rev 1a)$t$,
 'not yet', $t$not yet. FILL AT WRITE: written <time> CST on the operator's card (W4's thread; audit <id>): engine daf5da98 to <version> (Shared Library and L2 Count Plan), child 10624dd2 to <version> (Shared Library), Library 9a4d55c66bf65d7f. Read back by <seat> at Wall <id>. Offline (graded): both 41418 known bad lines raise K-GLS, the four known good glosses raise none, a K-GLS-only retraction is recorded and not applied, K-L2 output equal OLD and NEW (W2 10780, W3 10781). W4's pinned replay (plan criteria 7c, 7d, 7e, 8): not yet. Not yet shown by a run.$t$,
